  "chapterSummary": "Food security means people can obtain sufficient nutritious food. The chapter explains availability, accessibility and affordability and identifies groups vulnerable to food insecurity. India pursued foodgrain self-sufficiency and the Green Revolution increased production, especially of wheat and rice. The food-security system uses procurement, buffer stocks and the Public Distribution System. MSP supports procurement, issue prices support subsidised distribution, and Fair Price Shops provide access. Government programmes and cooperatives add further support.",
